    chore: upgrade to ESLint 10 flat config and lint all packages (#5220)
    
    * chore: add .editorconfig
    
    Keep line endings, final newlines, trailing whitespace and indentation
    consistent across editors for files clang-format does not cover.
    
    * chore: normalize whitespace to match .editorconfig
    
    Strip trailing whitespace and convert two CRLF files to LF. Markdown is
    left untouched since trailing spaces can be significant there.
    Whitespace-only change: git diff -w shows nothing.
    
    * chore: migrate ESLint to v10 flat config and lint all packages
    
    Replace the legacy .eslintrc.yaml/.eslintignore, which ESLint 9+ no
    longer reads and which ignored every package, with eslint.config.mjs.
    
    - eslint 10, @eslint/js and typescript-eslint recommended presets,
      eslint-plugin-wc best-practice, eslint-plugin-mocha recommended for
      tests
    - drop the deprecated eslint-config-google; clang-format owns formatting
    - no-explicit-any is a warning for now
    - mocha/no-mocha-arrows and no-unused-expressions are off in tests to
      match the arrow-function style and chai assertions
    - npm run lint now lints every package, including JS/MJS files
    
    * style: apply ESLint autofixes
    
    Output of `eslint . --fix` (curly, prefer-const, no-var,
    explicit-member-accessibility, no-wrapper-object-types, prefer-as-const,
    no-extra-boolean-cast, ...). Changed lines were reformatted with
    git-clang-format. Vendored third_party code is now ignored.
    
    * fix: resolve no-useless-escape and eqeqeq lint errors
    
    - drop unnecessary backslashes in regular expressions and strings
    - use strict equality; comparisons against undefined become == null to
      keep matching both null and undefined
    - dropdown compares Number(selected), since paper-listbox's selected
      may be a string
    
    * fix: resolve no-unused-vars and no-unused-expressions lint errors
    
    - super.x && super.x() becomes super.x?.()
    - use optional catch bindings where the error is unused
    - replace comma operators with statements in camera_settings
    - drop type-only $CombinedState imports; declarations still emit
    - use the Category interface instead of a placeholder constant
    - comment out imports only used by commented-out test-runner config
    
    * fix: resolve lint errors that point at real bugs
    
    - controls: keep the elapsed interaction-prompt time across visibility
      changes; it was reset on every call
    - validation: compare severityTitle instead of assigning it, so the
      glTF URL is only revoked after a conversion
    - exportScene: only wrap exporter.parse in the Promise, so errors from
      the awaited setup reject instead of leaving it pending; drop async
      from Promise executors that never await
    - custom-select example: set up shadow-DOM listeners once in the
      constructor and remove the document listener on disconnect
    - compare-results: read JSON with fs, as require() is unavailable in
      the ESM output
    - scene-graph-spec: the variant-revert tests returned from inside the
      search loop and never asserted; use break. The 'Yellow Red' case
      fails once it runs, so it is skipped with a TODO
    
    * fix: resolve remaining ESLint errors
    
    - wrap lexical declarations in case blocks
    - Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call instead of obj.hasOwnProperty
    - replace Function and {} types with specific types
    - assert non-null instead of mixing ?. with ! in tests
    - attach caught errors as cause (adds es2022.error lib to
      render-fidelity-tools)
    - drop unneeded @ts-ignore comments, this aliases, dead initial
      assignments and a full-width space
    - comment empty catch blocks
    - turn off no-unexpected-multiline, which conflicts with clang-format's
      layout of calls and tagged templates
    
    * ci: run ESLint in the unit-tests workflow
    
    Lint runs right after npm ci so it fails fast. Warnings
    (no-explicit-any) do not fail the build.
    
    * refactor: replace easy explicit any types
    
    - Lit update/updated overrides take Map<string|number|symbol, unknown>,
      matching existing usage; one caller now casts the old value
    - throttle/debounce are generic over the wrapped function's arguments
    - type render-fidelity configs as ImageComparisonConfig and let
      puppeteer/child_process handler types be inferred
    - catch bindings are unknown and cast to Error where .message is read
    - allow `...args: any[]` (ignoreRestArgs), which TypeScript mixins
      require
    
    no-explicit-any warnings: 269 -> 217.
    
    * refactor: type navigator.userAgentData instead of casting to any
    
    User-Agent Client Hints are missing from TypeScript's DOM lib, so
    declare the one method we use and move the XR form-factor check into a
    helper. Behavior is unchanged.
    
    * fix: keep published helper signatures unchanged
    
    lib/ is published and its .d.ts files are public. Restore the original
    throttle/debounce (any) and getValueOfEnum (T extends Object)
    signatures so callers that deep-import them are not broken by stricter
    types.
    
    * ci: pin GitHub Actions to commit SHAs
    
    The zizmor check fails on pull requests that change a workflow file
    containing actions referenced by tag. Pin every action to the commit
    its current tag points to, with the version in a comment, and give the
    read-only workflows an explicit `contents: read` permission.
    
    * test: un-skip and fix variant revert expectation in scene-graph-spec
    
